{"qid":"Q213638","names":["Kingdom of Cyprus"],"title":"Kingdom of Cyprus","endonym":{"native":"Βασίλειο της Κύπρου","lang":"el"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Cyprus was a Crusader state established in 1192 when Richard I of England sold the island to Guy of Lusignan, the dispossessed King of Jerusalem, after Richard had seized it from the Byzantine governor Isaac Komnenos during the Third Crusade. The Lusignan dynasty ruled Cyprus as a prosperous trading entrepôt between Europe and the Levant, and from 1268 also held the title King of Jerusalem; the kingdom reached its commercial zenith under Peter I (r. 1358–1369), who raided Alexandria in 1365. Venetian succession occurred when James II's widow Catherine Cornaro ceded Cyprus to Venice in 1489 following dynastic conflict; the dataset's end-date of 1492 reflects this transition. Venetian Cyprus fell to the Ottoman Empire in 1571.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Cyprus is an island with well-defined boundaries; territorial extent is precise throughout the period of Lusignan rule.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Cyprus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Cyprus"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Guy of Lusignan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_of_Lusignan"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Cyprus","rulers":[{"qid":"Q552405","name":"Hugh I of Cyprus","start":1205,"end":1218,"image":"GoldBezantHughIOfCyprus1205-1218.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/GoldBezantHughIOfCyprus1205-1218.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","artist":"PHGCOM","attribut